\f0\fs24 \cf0 This project acts a visualizer for a MIDI keyboard input. Sound is generated procedurally from input received by the MIDI in OnAudioFilterRead() using a sine wave, layered harmonics, and an ADSR envelope for each possible note played. \
\
A boids system is used to create the visualizer. The position of the boids will always follow the latest note pressed, but there are additional parameters. Sliding up and down on the Seaboard will cause the boids to rise and fall, and sliding left and right will incrementally shift the boids as well. A color circle is mapped to the frequency playing, and opacity is matched to amplitude. Playing multiple notes at once will also split the colors evenly among the boids, for example pressing 2 will cause one half to be one color, and the other half to be another. }